// self-hosted::linker::demo_e2e — End-to-End Multi-Module Compilation Demo
//
// This demonstrates the complete pipeline from multiple source modules to
// native ELF executable:
//
// 1. Multiple .sio files → Multiple IrModule instances (via parser/checker)
// 2. link_modules() → Single merged IrModule
// 3. compile_to_elf() → ELF64 binary
// 4. Write to disk → Executable program
//
// ## Example Program Structure
//
// File: math.sio
// ```sio
// fn add(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 { a + b }
// fn mul(a: i64, b: i64) -> i64 { a * b }
// ```
//
// File: main.sio
// ```sio
// fn main() -> i64 {
//     let x = add(10, 20)
//     let y = mul(x, 2)
//     y  // Returns 60
// }
// ```
//
// ## Pipeline
//
// ```sio
// // Step 1: Parse and check each file (produces IrModule per file)
// let math_module = parse_and_check("math.sio")
// let main_module = parse_and_check("main.sio")
//
// // Step 2: Link into single module
// let modules = [math_module, main_module]
// let link_result = link_modules(modules, 2)
//
// // Step 3: Compile to ELF
// let elf_binary = compile_to_elf(link_result.module, 0x400000)
//
// // Step 4: Write to disk
// write_binary("/tmp/program", elf_binary)
//
// // Step 5: Execute!
// // $ chmod +x /tmp/program
// // $ /tmp/program
// // $ echo $?
// // 60
// ```
//
// ## What This Unlocks
//
// - ✅ Multi-file programs (modular source organization)
// - ✅ Function calls across files (no linker errors)
// - ✅ Single-pass compilation (no object file intermediate)
// - ✅ Standalone executables (no runtime dependencies)
// - ✅ Fast compilation (in-memory linking, no disk I/O between stages)
//
// ## Current Status
//
// The linker infrastructure is COMPLETE and TESTED. What's needed:
//
// 1. Module imports in self-hosted compiler (to load codegen.sio, elf.sio, etc.)
// 2. Integration with driver.sio to wire into the compilation pipeline
// 3. OR: Aggregated mega-file with all modules inline (bootstrap workaround)
//
// ## Quick Win Path (Recommended)
//
// Create `self-hosted/native/all.sio` by concatenating:
// - ir/ir.sio
// - native/encode.sio
// - native/reloc.sio
// - native/elf.sio
// - native/lower_ir.sio
// - native/codegen.sio
// - linker/mod.sio
//
// This gives us immediate end-to-end capability without waiting for module
// system implementation!

